cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HaanJi in research, please cite it as below."
title: "HaanJi: a voice receptionist for Indian small businesses that hears the business's own words, answers before the caller finishes, and can prove what was agreed"
type: software
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-29"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/aritra-25hazra/haanji"
url: "https://github.com/aritra-25hazra/haanji"
abstract: >-
  An open-source voice-agent engine for Hinglish, Benglish and Marathinglish
  callers with three measured mechanisms: Bhasha Bridge (a per-tenant phonetic
  index that biases the recogniser and repairs its output under a two-condition
  rule that cannot damage a correct transcript), Speculative Turn Execution
  (read-only tools predicted and run from partial transcripts, claimed only on
  byte-identical arguments) and the Pramaan Ledger (Ed25519-signed, hash-chained
  consent receipts with daily Merkle anchors that refuse unconfirmed writes).
  The evaluation harness, the real-recogniser pipeline, the baselines and the
  report are in the repository.
keywords:
  - voice agent
  - speech recognition
  - Hinglish
  - code-mixed speech
  - phonetic matching
  - contextual biasing
  - speculative execution
  - verifiable receipts
  - small business
  - India
authors:
